- action(n1, "start computer repair process"): The source integrates initiation and the first task into a single directive ("To initiate the computer repair process, begin by examining the hardware"); extracting it as a standalone action hallucinates an extra procedural step not present in the description.
- action(n6, "is system functioning properly"): The source describes a conditional evaluation branching directly from the test step ("If the test results indicate..."), not a distinct process activity. Modeling it as a separate action inserts an unwarranted intermediate node in the control flow, violating direct source chronology.